  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "transferBadPixelsToMap",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/RawImage.cpp",
    "description": "`RawImageData::transferBadPixelsToMap()` trusts entries in `mBadPixelPositions` and uses `assert(pos_x < (ushort16)uncropped_dim.x)` / `assert(pos_y < (ushort16)uncropped_dim.y)` as bounds checks. For this PoV, decoding produces at least one bad-pixel coordinate outside the uncropped image dimensions, so the assertion at line 320 fires and aborts. The crash is an assertion-based abort, not a sanitizer-detected memory corruption.",
    "conditions": "In the `TiffDecoderFuzzer-DngDecoder` harness, attacker-controlled TIFF/DNG bytes are parsed and passed to `decoder->decodeRaw()`, which calls `RawDecoder::decodeRaw()` -> `raw->fixBadPixels()` -> `transferBadPixelsToMap()`. If crafted metadata causes invalid bad-pixel positions to be recorded in `mBadPixelPositions` (e.g., x/y beyond `uncropped_dim`), `transferBadPixelsToMap()` hits the assert and aborts. Trigger requires bad-pixel interpolation path enabled (`interpolateBadPixels` true in decode flow) and malformed bad-pixel coordinates from input."
  },
